<title>UK: INTERVIEW - LASMO sees $19 Brent in 1997.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW - LASMO sees $19 Brent in 1997.</headline>
<byline>Tim Farrand</byline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>British oil exploration company LASMO Plc expects oil prices to weaken in the short term but Brent crude should average $19 for the year, chief executive Joe Darby said in an interview.</p>
<p>&quot;We think prices are going to weaken in the short term, but we don't think they are going to fall through the floor, the floor being around $15 or $16 a barrel,&quot; said Darby</p>
<p>&quot;We are planning on $19 average for the year on Brent.&quot; LASMO realised an average $18.72 per barrel in 1996, up from $17.09 in 1995.</p>
</text>
